.TH DEBUG 4 2026-10-06 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
debug, debug_subsystem.SUBSYSTEM \- Lustre debug log message masks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.B lctl get_param debug
.SY
.B lctl set_param debug=
.RI { FLAG_LIST | HEX_MASK }
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param debug=+" FLAG
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param debug=-" FLAG
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param debug_subsystem." SUBSYSTEM
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param debug_subsystem." SUBSYSTEM =
.RI { FLAG_LIST | HEX_MASK }
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Global
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB debug= "warning+error+emerg+console+neterror+ha+config+ioctl+lfsck"
.br
.BI debug_subsystem. SUBSYSTEM =0
.RB "(inherit " debug )
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B debug
parameter is the global mask of message classes that
.BR CDEBUG ()
calls in the kernel are allowed to log.
A message is kept only if its class is set in the applicable mask --
.B debug
itself, or a nonzero per-subsystem override that replaces it (see
.B debug_subsystem.SUBSYSTEM
below) -- and its subsystem is set in
.BR subsystem_debug (4).
.PP
.I FLAG_LIST
is a comma, space, or plus-separated list of flag names, or a
.I HEX_MASK
(hexadecimal or decimal number);
a non-zero, non-all-ones
.I HEX_MASK
is deprecated and logs a warning.
A
.RI "leading " + " or " -
adds or removes flags from the current mask instead of replacing it.
The value
.B 0
clears the mask so that only the mandatory classes below are logged;
the keyword
.BR all " or the value " -1
enables every class, and
.B default
restores the default mask shown above.
.PP
The following classes are supported, with the approximate overhead of
enabling each one continuously on a busy server
.RB ( low ", " medium " or " high ).
A class marked
.B "(always)"
is always logged, whatever
.B debug
is set to; one marked
.B "(default)"
is part of the default mask above, but can still be masked out.
.TP
.BR trace " (high)"
Function entry/exit markers logged by
.BR ENTRY " and " EXIT
and direct
.BR CDEBUG ( D_TRACE )
callers.
.TP
.BR inode " (medium)"
Inode-level operations.
.TP
.BR super " (low)"
Superblock and mount/umount operations.
.TP
.BR iotrace " (low)"
Simple, low-overhead I/O tracing of read and write calls.
.TP
.BR malloc " (high)"
Logs every memory allocation and free.
.TP
.BR cache " (medium)"
Cache-related operations (e.g. page and lock caches).
.TP
.BR info " (medium)"
General informational messages.
.TP
.BR ioctl " (low, default)"
.BR ioctl (2)
request handling.
.TP
.BR neterror " (low, default)"
Network errors.
.TP
.BR net " (high)"
Network communication, logged for most RPCs sent and received.
.TP
.BR warning " (low, always)"
.BR CWARN ()
messages.
Always logged regardless of the
.B debug
mask.
.TP
.BR buffs " (medium)"
Buffer handling.
.TP
.BR other " (medium)"
Miscellaneous messages that do not fit another class.
.TP
.BR dentry " (medium)"
Dentry-level operations.
.TP
.BR nettrace " (high)"
Detailed network tracing, more verbose than
.BR net .
.TP
.BR page " (high)"
Bulk page handling for I/O.
.TP
.BR dlmtrace " (medium)"
Distributed Lock Manager (DLM) operations.
.TP
.BR error " (low, always)"
.BR CERROR ()
messages.
Always logged regardless of the
.B debug
mask.
.TP
.BR emerg " (low, always)"
.BR CEMERG ()
messages for serious, urgent conditions.
Always logged regardless of the
.B debug
mask.
.TP
.BR ha " (low, default)"
Recovery and failover events.
.TP
.BR rpctrace " (high)"
Detailed per-RPC tracing, for distributed debugging.
.TP
.BR vfstrace " (high)"
VFS-level operation tracing.
.TP
.BR reada " (medium)"
Read-ahead decisions and activity.
.TP
.BR mmap " (medium)"
.BR mmap (2)
related operations.
.TP
.BR config " (low, default)"
Configuration log processing.
.TP
.BR console " (low, always)"
Messages that are also sent to the system console.
Always logged regardless of the
.B debug
mask.
.TP
.BR quota " (medium)"
Quota accounting and enforcement.
.TP
.BR sec " (medium)"
Security and upcall cache operations.
.TP
.BR lfsck " (low, default)"
OI scrub and LFSCK activity.
.TP
.BR hsm " (low)"
Hierarchical Storage Management (HSM) coordinator activity.
.TP
.BR snapshot " (low)"
Snapshot creation and management.
.TP
.BR layout " (medium)"
File layout and mirror handling, including FLR.
.PP
Since release 2.18.0, the
.B debug
mask can be overridden per subsystem with
.BR debug_subsystem.SUBSYSTEM (4),
so that, for example,
.B osc
can log
.B iotrace
independently of
.BR llite " and " mdc .
A subsystem whose override is
.B 0
inherits
.B debug
unchanged; writing
.B none
to the override disables all non-mandatory classes for that subsystem only.
Once an override is nonzero it is a fixed copy, not a live link: a later
change to
.B debug
does not reach that subsystem until its override is set back to
.BR 0 " or " default .
.SH EXAMPLES
Enable RPC and DLM tracing everywhere:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl set_param debug=+rpctrace+dlmtrace"
.EE
.PP
Reset to the default mask:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl set_param debug=default"
.EE
.PP
Enable I/O tracing on OSC only, leaving the global mask alone:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl set_param debug_subsystem.osc=+iotrace"
.EE
.PP
Go back to inheriting the global mask on OSC:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl set_param debug_subsystem.osc=0"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B debug
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 0.7.0,
.\" commit 0.7.0-0-g96ec6856f9
but per-subsystem overrides with
.BR debug_subsystem.SUBSYSTEM (4)
are only available since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit 2.17.6x
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR debug_mb (4),
.BR debug_path (4),
.BR printk (4),
.BR subsystem_debug (4),
.BR subsystem_printk (4),
.BR lctl-clear (8),
.BR lctl-debug_daemon (8),
.BR lctl-debug_kernel (8),
.BR lctl-dk (8),
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
